{"signature": "{\"text\": \"A useful approach is to identify the unwanted transfer, explain which energy store increases and choose a method that reduces the transfer. Lubrication forms a layer between moving surfaces and reduces friction. Streamlining can reduce air resistance, which is another force opposing motion. Thermal insulation reduces the rate of energy transfer between places at different temperatures. In electrical circuits, lower-resistance conductors can reduce energy dissipated by heating for a given current, although practical design also depends on cost and safety.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 33.936, "words": [["A", 0.102083], ["useful", 0.258333], ["approach", 0.596875], ["is", 1.026583], ["to", 1.169791], ["identify", 1.313041], ["the", 1.964083], ["unwanted", 2.042208], ["transfer,", 2.55], ["explain", 3.279166], ["which", 3.721875], ["energy", 3.930208], ["store", 4.333875], ["increases", 4.594291], ["and", 5.089083], ["choose", 5.284375], ["a", 5.50575], ["method", 5.583875], ["that", 5.948458], ["reduces", 6.169791], ["the", 6.651583], ["transfer.", 6.794791], ["Lubrication", 8.203125], ["forms", 8.90625], ["a", 9.244791], ["layer", 9.322916], ["between", 9.648458], ["moving", 9.973958], ["surfaces", 10.273458], ["and", 10.807291], ["reduces", 10.963541], ["friction.", 11.432291], ["Streamlining", 12.851583], ["can", 13.567708], ["reduce", 13.75], ["air", 14.088541], ["resistance,", 14.257833], ["which", 15.208333], ["is", 15.403666], ["another", 15.494791], ["force", 15.833333], ["opposing", 16.106791], ["motion.", 16.523458], ["Thermal", 17.851583], ["insulation", 18.216166], ["reduces", 18.815125], ["the", 19.309916], ["rate", 19.440125], ["of", 19.6745], ["energy", 19.856791], ["transfer", 20.273458], ["between", 20.690125], ["places", 21.028666], ["at", 21.39325], ["different", 21.575541], ["temperatures.", 21.940125], ["In", 23.645833], ["electrical", 23.828125], ["circuits,", 2